{
  "id": "21038_karikomu",
  "headword": "{刈|か}り{込|こ}む",
  "reading": "かりこむ",
  "romaji": "karikomu",
  "part_of_speech": "godan verb, transitive",
  "gloss": "to trim; to clip; to prune into shape",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to trim; to clip; to prune into shape",
      "explanation": "To cut plants, hedges, or hair short and neatly, shaping them by cutting into the body of the growth."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21038_karikomu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{生垣|いけがき}を{刈|か}り{込|こ}む。",
      "english": "To trim the hedge.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21038_karikomu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{庭師|にわし}が{松|まつ}の{木|き}をきれいに{刈|か}り{込|こ}んだ。",
      "english": "The gardener neatly trimmed the pine tree.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21038_karikomu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{芝生|しばふ}を{短|みじか}く{刈|か}り{込|こ}んで、{庭|にわ}が{見違|みちが}えるようになった。",
      "english": "After trimming the lawn short, the garden looked completely different.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound verb from {刈|か}る (to mow, cut) + {込|こ}む (into, deeply). The ～{込|こ}む suffix adds the nuance of cutting into and shaping, not just cutting the surface.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {生垣|いけがき}を{刈|か}り{込|こ}む: to trim a hedge\n- {芝生|しばふ}を{刈|か}り{込|こ}む: to trim the lawn\n- {植木|うえき}を{刈|か}り{込|こ}む: to trim garden trees\n- {丸|まる}く{刈|か}り{込|こ}む: to trim into a round shape\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {刈|か}る: to mow, to cut — basic cutting without the shaping nuance\n- {刈|か}り{取|と}る: to harvest, to cut down — focuses on cutting and gathering, used for crops\n- {剪定|せんてい}する: to prune — formal gardening term for cutting branches to improve growth\n- {整|ととの}える: to tidy, to arrange — more general term for making things neat",
